      "usage": {
        "input_tokens": 45123,
        "output_tokens": 517,
        "calls": 3,
        "seconds": 15.03
      },
      "text": "A player is in an offside position if they are in the opponents' half and ahead of both the ball and the second-last opponent when a teammate plays or touches the ball. Hands and arms don't count; level is onside. Position alone isn't an offence — the player must then interfere with play or an opponent, or gain an advantage from a rebound, deflection or save. Direct reception from a throw-in, corner or goal kick is exempt. A deliberate opponent play generally resets the situation; a deliberate save does not. The sanction is an indirect free kick.",
